<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v2.3 20070202//EN" "archivearticle.dtd"><article xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" article-type="research-article"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">Yeast</journal-id><journal-title>Yeast (Chichester, England)</journal-title><issn pub-type="ppub">0749-503X</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1097-0061</issn><publisher><publisher-name>Hindawi Publishing Corporation</publisher-name></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmid">11119303</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2448391</article-id>		<article-id pub-id-type="pii">S1531691200000371</article-id>		<article-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/1097-0061(200012)17:4&#x0003c;263::AID-YEA44&#x0003e;3.0.CO;2-G</article-id>	<article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Research Article</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>		<italic>Xylella</italic> Genomics and Bacterial Pathogenicity to Plants</article-title></title-group><contrib-group>		<contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Dow</surname><given-names>J.  M.</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff1">1</xref></contrib>		<contrib contrib-type="author" corresp="yes"><name><surname>Daniels</surname><given-names>M.  J.</given-names></name><address><email>mike.daniels@bbsrc.ac.uk</email></address></contrib>	</contrib-group>		<aff id="aff1"><label>1</label>			<addr-line>The Sainsbury Laboratory</addr-line>			<addr-line>John Innes Centre</addr-line>			<addr-line>Norwich Research Park</addr-line>			<addr-line>Colney</addr-line>			<addr-line>Norwich</addr-line>			<addr-line>NR4 7UH</addr-line>			<country>UK</country>		</aff>	<pub-date pub-type="ppub"><year>2000</year></pub-date><volume>17</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>263</fpage><lpage>271</lpage><history><date date-type="received"><day>21</day><month>9</month><year>2000</year></date><date date-type="accepted"><day>21</day><month>9</month><year>2000</year></date></history><permissions><copyright-statement>Copyright &#x000a9; 2000 Hindawi Publishing Corporation.</copyright-statement><copyright-year>2000</copyright-year><copyright-holder>Hindawi Publishing Corporation</copyright-holder><license license-type="open-access" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/"><p>This is an open access article distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution License, which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original work is properly cited.</p></license></permissions><abstract>		<p>			<italic>Xylella fastidiosa</italic>, a pathogen of citrus, is the first plant pathogenic bacterium for which the complete genome sequence has been published. Inspection of the sequence reveals high relatedness to many genes of other pathogens, notably <italic>Xanthomonas campestris</italic>. Based on this, we suggest that <italic>Xylella</italic> possesses certain easily testable properties that contribute to pathogenicity. We also present some general considerations for deriving information on pathogenicity from bacterial genomics.</p>	</abstract></article-meta></front></article>